  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Living with History, 1914-1964 (2021), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 3 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 1,637 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Living with History, 1914-1964 by Nicholas Bullock and Luc Verpoest was published by Leuven University Press in 2021. Conceptually, the work connects to Historiography, Urbanism, Context (archaeology), Architecture and History.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 3 citations. Notable citing venues include Urban Geography, Studia z Dziejów Rosji i Europy Środkowo-Wschodniej and The urban book series. The citing works include 2 journal articles and 1 book chapter. They come from 3 countries, led by the United Kingdom, Poland and the United States.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 1,637 times via OAPEN. Its subject matter aligns with Sustainable cities and communities among the Sustainable Development Goals.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\" data-wiki-books=\"verified\">The latest English Wikipedia check verified 2 article–work reference matches. These are references or bibliography entries, which may include other editions of the same work; they do not measure readership.</p>\n",
